# Cal.com Clone Project Tasks

## Phase 1: Project setup & MySQL database design (~1.5 hrs)
- [x] Create Next.js project with TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- [x] Provision MySQL 8 database — use PlanetScale (free) or Railway MySQL instance
- [x] Install Prisma, set provider to "mysql" in schema.prisma, add DATABASE_URL to .env
- [x] Design full schema: users, event_types, availability, bookings — with proper MySQL data types
- [x] Use INT AUTO_INCREMENT or CHAR(36) for IDs — avoid UUID() issues in MySQL foreign keys
- [x] Run prisma migrate dev to apply schema, then run seed script
- [x] Seed: 1 default user, 3 event types, 5 sample bookings with varied statuses
> [!NOTE]  
> MySQL-specific: Use ENUM('active','cancelled') for booking status. Use TIME columns for availability slots. Use TINYINT(1) for boolean flags (e.g. is_available). Prisma handles these natively with the mysql provider.

## Phase 2: Backend API routes (~2.5 hrs)
- [x] GET /api/event-types — list all event types
- [x] POST /api/event-types — create new event type
- [x] PUT /api/event-types/:id — edit event type
- [x] DELETE /api/event-types/:id — delete event type
- [x] GET/PUT /api/availability — fetch and update availability schedule
- [x] GET /api/slots/:slug/:date — compute free time slots for a date
- [x] POST /api/bookings — create booking with double-booking check using MySQL transaction
- [x] GET /api/bookings — list all bookings split by upcoming/past
- [x] PATCH /api/bookings/:id/cancel — set status = 'cancelled' in MySQL
- [x] GET /api/booking/:id/confirm — return booking details for confirmation page
> [!NOTE]  
> Double-booking prevention in MySQL: wrap the check + insert in a Prisma transaction with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE to lock the row. This prevents race conditions — important with MySQL's InnoDB engine.

## Phase 3: Admin dashboard (event types + availability) (~2.5 hrs)
- [x] Build Cal.com-style sidebar layout with nav: Event Types, Availability, Bookings
- [x] Event Types page — list as cards with copy-link, edit, delete actions
- [x] Create / Edit Event Type modal — title, description, duration, URL slug fields
- [x] Availability page — day toggles (Mon-Sun), time range pickers, timezone selector
- [x] Bookings dashboard — tabs for Upcoming / Past, cancel button per booking
- [x] Match Cal.com visual design: white sidebar, minimal cards, clean typography
> [!TIP]  
> Study cal.com's actual dashboard before building. Key UI: event type cards with a link icon, per-day availability toggles, clean bookings table.

## Phase 4: Public booking page (~3 hrs)
- [x] Route: `/[username]/[slug]` — fully public, no login required
- [x] Left panel: event info (title, duration, timezone)
- [x] Calendar grid — disable days with no availability set in MySQL availability table
- [x] Time slot list — fetched from /api/slots, excludes already-booked slots from MySQL
- [x] Booking form: booker name, email — submits to POST /api/bookings
- [x] Confirmation page /booking/confirmed?id=... — query booking by ID from MySQL
> [!TIP]  
> Most visible part — evaluators will use this directly. Match Cal.com's 3-column booking layout exactly. Use react-day-picker for the calendar.

## Phase 5: Bonus features (if time permits) (optional)
- [ ] Responsive design — mobile and tablet layouts with Tailwind breakpoints
- [ ] Email notifications via Resend or Nodemailer on booking confirmation/cancellation
- [ ] Rescheduling flow — update booking's date/time, check slot availability in MySQL
- [ ] Buffer time — add buffer_after_minutes column to event_types table
- [ ] Date overrides table — MySQL table for blocked dates or custom hour ranges
> [!IMPORTANT]  
> Only attempt after all 4 core modules are working end-to-end. A polished core is far better than broken bonus features.

## Phase 6: Deployment + README + submission (~1 hr)
- [ ] Deploy frontend to Vercel — add DATABASE_URL (MySQL connection string) as env var
- [ ] MySQL DB on PlanetScale or Railway — run prisma migrate deploy + seed on production
- [ ] Write README: setup steps, MySQL config, env vars list, assumptions made
- [ ] Make GitHub repo public, test full booking flow on live URL end-to-end
- [ ] Submit GitHub link + deployed app link
> [!NOTE]  
> In your README, explicitly mention MySQL 8 as the database. Include the Prisma schema snippet and note any MySQL-specific decisions (ENUM types, TIME columns, InnoDB transactions) — this shows DB awareness to evaluators.
